From 5847b27306f17c7f1e14ae7edf114c8ab01812bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:13:16 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Don't deadlock when playback is stopped while an OK
 dialog is open

An input stream add-on can show an OK dialog from Open() on the
VideoPlayer thread, e.g. inputstream.adaptive when it can't download the
manifest. If a stop comes while that dialog is open, the app thread
handles it inside the dialog's render loop and waits in CloseFile() for
the VideoPlayer thread, which is waiting for the dialog, so Kodi hangs.

ShowOKDialogText() and ShowOKDialogLines() now stop waiting once the
stop event of the calling CThread is set, and later calls from that
thread return at once. The dialog stays open until it is dismissed. The
message owns the dialog text through a new SendMsgAbortable() overload,
as the app thread may still read it after the sender has gone, and
CThread::GetStopEvent() is now public for the helper.

Assisted-by: Claude
