From d9b4c7c1dd378820a9d2bfea2620d5265b0e92b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:13:16 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Close a modal dialog when the thread waiting for it is
 stopped

CGUIDialog::Open() from another thread waits for the dialog to close,
so Kodi hangs the same way when playback is stopped while an add-on's
Select or other modal dialog is open on the VideoPlayer thread, e.g.
inputstream.adaptive's quality chooser.

Open() now stops waiting when the stop event of the calling CThread is
set, like the OK dialog. Nothing reads the answer after that, so the
dialog closes on its next frame. That also covers dialogs the caller
deletes once Open() returns, like the file browser.

Assisted-by: Claude
